Scope of the MIT license in LICENSE
===================================

The MIT license covers this plugin's own source code.

It does NOT cover the OpenCode tool definitions the plugin sends at runtime
(opencode_tools.json). That file is a separate work, originating from OpenCode's
CLI. The copy this plugin was verified against came from opencode2api, which is
GPL-3.0-or-later.

Because of that, the definitions are not distributed here: not in the source
tree and not embedded in the compiled library. The plugin downloads them on the
operator's own machine at registration and caches them there, which is the same
thing fetch-tools.sh does by hand. See README_CN.md, "工具定义数据（不在本仓库里）".

Nothing in this repository is derived from opencode2api's implementation. The
plugin was written against the observed behaviour of the free-tier gate.
